<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for Enhancement Shaman DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic for Phase 3. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from Heroics, reputation rewards, and the new 10-man Raid loot added to Titan Rune Dungeons.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot-gear">Enhancement Shaman DPS Best in Slot Gear, Gems, and Enchants - Pre-Raid Phase 3</h2>Enhancement <a class="icontiny c7" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/shaman">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_shaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shaman</span></a> Tier 8 set has decent bonuses, making it worth using even with  the lower item level available within pre-raid gear constraints.<br/>
<br/>The main concern when looking for pre-raid gear is using the limited stat budget to get as many useful stats as possible, while also hitting the Hit and Expertise caps.<br/>
<br/>In Wrath, 26.23 Hit Rating converts into 1% Spell Hit at level 70. Unfortunately, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30819/dual-wield-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwieldspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dual Wield Specialization</span></a> does <b>not</b> give Spell Hit, thus the cap is 17% Spell Hit from gear alone, which can be reduced to 14% (or 13% if you are Alliance due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a>) with the help of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33602/improved-faerie-fire">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_faeriefire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Improved Faerie Fire</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=33193/misery">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_misery.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Misery</span></a>. Thus, the exact amount of Spell Hit you want from your gear depends on the content you are optimizing for, and your faction. As a Horde player in a raid, you will need 26.23 * 14 = 	367.22 rating in order to cap Spell Hit, for example.<br/>
<br/>You will also be well over the 8% special attack melee Hit cap by then, as although 32.78 Hit Rating is required for 1%, you get 6% for free with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=30819/dual-wield-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwieldspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dual Wield Specialization</span></a>, thus only needing 32.78 * 2 = 65.56 rating. Extra Hit rating over specials cap will still increase your white hit damage and enable more <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=51532/maelstrom-weapon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shaman_maelstromweapon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maelstrom Weapon</span></a> procs, which is a decent benefit. <br/>
<br/>Take note that the <b>Hit cap is a limiter to Hit's usefulness</b>, instead of a mandatory goal to attain at any cost. While Hit has great value until the cap, using gear with overall better stats is better than being Hit capped with bad gear.<br/>
<br/>
